[{"id":"VRCE-4-43-1","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":43,"verse":1,"english":"Sugrīva had declared his conviction that he relied particularly upon Hanumān.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.886,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-44-1"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4043001","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"9dc6ba4e9722992f4eb1b8bca0377258b6586f62f2cd21bdc60d01a2ee38863d","compact":"984d6c328197959624be59e59c5da6fc0fddcf8669d7b7cd2a912a10a74d2cde","nasal":"984d6c328197959624be59e59c5da6fc0fddcf8669d7b7cd2a912a10a74d2cde"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-43-2","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":43,"verse":2,"english":"O foremost of monkeys, neither on the earth, nor in the sky', nor in the etherial regions, nor yet in water, find I any obstacle to your course. 1. Antariksa-regions above the earth in which the birds fly. 2. Ambara— Upper air.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.81,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-44-3"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4043002","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"d7f93b2eae3c4af06ce586d645851990ddd0a6ade0bb7c383ff7bc21a9210055","compact":"164995fce32fbd29b1691062c7909e416299de6e657c137d7ba550bfb01b7195","nasal":"22d728e19f7e3ee2cda75209b71b4146f523be6259c0f8c9c1751ae1bc08ef8c"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-43-3","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":43,"verse":3,"english":"The entire worlds with Asuras, and Gandharvas, and Nāgas, and men, and gods, with oceans, and the earth and the regions beneath—are well known to you.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.852,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-44-4"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4043003","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"878d64e0f34a7980789cea6ed9ee4feb722ebf182d39ca1674ef9dfcbc3df6ba","compact":"d304790a97546d924d21f78e3ee49781abc82fd57e2b4c5decb8e8c21a28c321","nasal":"de40e19ba334d291569f4e0a2d3861504954c25f7576bd46ca05e6a44c52653c"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-43-4","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":43,"verse":4,"english":"And your motion, vehemence, energy and fleetness, are, O hero, O mighty ape, even like those of your sire, the powerful wind god; and there exists no creature on earth that is like to you in energy. Therefore do you bethink you how Sītā may be recovered.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-44-5"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4043004","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"b43e46704dd8be8814a50880afd26aa623621515783d4e0611a7c1be8a5a203a","compact":"0605ebf4b3f6e75aaac388e927cc1607548f37477b5ae9cbb1425c93e7189ff9","nasal":"0605ebf4b3f6e75aaac388e927cc1607548f37477b5ae9cbb1425c93e7189ff9"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-43-5","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":43,"verse":5,"english":"And your motion, vehemence, energy and fleetness, are, O hero, O mighty ape, even like those of your sire, the powerful wind god; and there exists no creature on earth that is like to you in energy. Therefore do you bethink you how Sītā may be recovered.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.611,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-44-5"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4043005","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"5e0794b0312b11b910b19a8de9cff2a28f4f02c75574492caf316fa420b265ed","compact":"a8210dbf3130542450579d4a43f024ef3bb4c40d5023cfe61d5764b5001e6868","nasal":"a8210dbf3130542450579d4a43f024ef3bb4c40d5023cfe61d5764b5001e6868"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-43-6","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":43,"verse":6,"english":"Even in you, O you versed in policy, are strength, and wit, and courage, and policy, and conduct in consonance with season and place.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.883,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-44-6"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4043006","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"6e4c968d77ef86ae87ff9f0d01e9d4be795fcf8759d99e3e07816d3ac218bef3","compact":"48ab307e9bc84478446c5e27d89a595fc2b29984eda5bef1d42fd54e15fc6e1b","nasal":"47bb18f40b9294f74e95501de1a9e633c44fec29243c263377d53da32f447457"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-43-7","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":43,"verse":7,"english":"Thereat, understanding that success in the task depended upon Hanumān, and also knowing what Hanumān was, Rāghava reflected,","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.843,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-44-7"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4043007","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"4752bd8c26e2c9860f18861bb7cc9ec3e42fe7abaf5c44555fb13d06e0057e31","compact":"ccfd295b5b7216d08b189545ca8151b7902afae3f4ecc0d0d7cb08b5e7fad01d","nasal":"a88128b375be5c3069453396002400ab9b953f2b462996ab64ca409c4ec369c8"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-43-8","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":43,"verse":8,"english":"This lord of monkeys is every way confident concerning Hanumān; and Hanumān himself is even more confident of achieving success in the work.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-44-8"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4043008","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"328cbd589faf9701fcacd188e8e057a28aa170d6e231fbc5d676975aae91deb1","compact":"f6aa320871c61f3fee9639b946be496bca59d050424c5e634a79f21b7aed8b66","nasal":"f6aa320871c61f3fee9639b946be496bca59d050424c5e634a79f21b7aed8b66"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-43-9","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":43,"verse":9,"english":"He that has been tested by his deed, and who has been considered worthiest by his master, having veen commissioned in this business,-success in the work is certain.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.773,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-44-9"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4043009","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"384a631217f839a34afd7ad45871ebb4a77f402201c7f29c06a32689c4810ca0","compact":"0e86975996e48d160877849a983c76413c57f9535bad4e2a587366a113eb40b3","nasal":"0e86975996e48d160877849a983c76413c57f9535bad4e2a587366a113eb40b3"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-43-10","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":43,"verse":10,"english":"Then beholding that monkey who was the fittest for the task, that exceedingly energetic senses one, (Rāma), with his mind and exhilarated, considering himself as already crowned with success, felt the excess of joy.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.818,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-44-10"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4043010","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"613ab90f22be34307f7e6c7cfc485fe9fb913e5b221dc08ea0f256a58c182164","compact":"b6d8ed1f2da69bfe5ed153b60a8ebd08d59614e469d85765dffc5fe5ebba881a","nasal":"d3fa67574e65bade6abac3e3111e7b576aa231091daf070e99143b6a55cfd962"}},{"id":"VRCE-4-43-11","kanda":4,"kandaId":"kishkindha","sarga":43,"verse":11,"english":"And well pleased, that subduer of enemies handed to Hanuman a ring inscribed with his name, as a sign to the king's daughter.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-4-44-11"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"4043011","sanskritFile":"Ram04.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"d4ef8f8ca1d2ec66cb51cc2f0449db30140404eae022bb